# Atlas graph

Import NodeRecord from "./node_record.lg".
Import RankScore from "./rank_score.lg".
Import RankTrail from "./rank_trail.lg".
Import TrailDigest from "./trail_digest.lg".
Import OpdpRow from "./opdp_row.lg".

The atlas graph above the problems, built while rows stream past: each cohort,
collection and category once, in first-seen order, each ranked by its best
problem, so the graph orders its branches by where the most promising work is.

## An AtlasGraph has:
    an ids, which is Seq of Text.
    a nodes, which is Map of Text to Node.

## To newAtlasGraph () -> AtlasGraph:
    Return a new AtlasGraph with ids [] and nodes (a new Map of Text to Node).

## Note
A row's rank before anything has been tried on it.

## To rowRank (row: OpdpRow) -> Int:
    Return priority(row's inputs, noSignals()).

## Note
The graph with node `id` raised to at least `rank`, made the first time.

## To raiseNode (g: AtlasGraph, node: Node) -> AtlasGraph:
    Let mutable nodes be g's nodes.
    Let mutable ids be g's ids.
    If ids contains node's id:
        Let mutable known be item (node's id) of nodes.
        If node's rank is greater than known's rank:
            Set known's rank to node's rank.
            Set nodes at node's id to known.
    Otherwise:
        Push node's id to ids.
        Set nodes at node's id to node.
    Return a new AtlasGraph with ids ids and nodes nodes.

## Note
The graph with a row's cohort, collection and category raised to its rank.

## To graphWithRow (g: AtlasGraph, row: OpdpRow) -> AtlasGraph:
    Let p be row's problem.
    Let rank be rowRank(row).
    Let cohort be cohortNodeId(p's cohort).
    Let collection be collectionNodeId(p's cohort, row's collectionSlug).
    Let mutable label be row's collectionLabel.
    If label is equal to "":
        Set label to row's collectionSlug.
    Let mutable out be raiseNode(g, rankedNode(cohort, none, none, "cohort", p's cohort, rank)).
    Set out to raiseNode(out, rankedNode(collection, some cohort, none, "collection", label, rank)).
    Let category be categoryNodeId(p's cohort, row's collectionSlug, row's categorySlug).
    Return raiseNode(out, rankedNode(category, some collection, none, "category", row's categoryLabel, rank)).

## Note
A row's own node, under its category.

## To rowNode (row: OpdpRow) -> Node:
    Let p be row's problem.
    Let parent be categoryNodeId(p's cohort, row's collectionSlug, row's categorySlug).
    Return rankedNode(problemNodeId(p's id), some parent, some p's id, "problem", p's title, rowRank(row)).

## Note
The graph's nodes, parents before children.

## To graphNodes (g: AtlasGraph) -> Seq of Node:
    Let mutable out be a new Seq of Node.
    Repeat for kind in ["cohort", "collection", "category"]:
        Repeat for id in g's ids:
            If (item id of g's nodes)'s kind is equal to kind:
                Push item id of g's nodes to out.
    Return out.
